====================================================================================================================
VERDICT
====================================================================================================================
  The live H_S readout works as an instrument: FP13's ramp holds exactly, the operator uses the readout it takes each step, and the LCDM boxes show how far a mesh's 'actual field' is from FP13's halofit stand-in (D3).  No H_S number here is physics: XR18 finds H_S ill-posed as written at z <= 0.635, a force this quasi-static box does not contain.

  4/4 checks pass; load-bearing failures: 0; wrote XR21_s1_hs_readout_results.json   [1139 s]
